+# catches it on purpose has to be run by something -- that is what this line is
+# for, and `ci.yml`'s `tests` job already runs the same tool through its suite.
+# What this adds is the tier, not the coverage.
+# Each anchor is a string of the tool's own source rather than a rank into a
+# growing file, so a citation that has drifted is reported with the anchor's
+# current line beside it -- one edit rather than a re-measurement.
+# Cheap tier because of what it reads: five markdown files, one Python file, the
+# standard library, no firmware image, no Ghidra, no network, no assembler.
+#
+# This function sits here, with the other `check_*` functions, because this
+# boundary is free: no other prepared patch in `docs/ci/` carries a pre-image
